<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Achmea posts nearly 18 pct higher H1 profit.</title>
<headline>Dutch Achmea posts nearly 18 pct higher H1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>ZEIST, Netherlands 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    318.6  vs   270.3</p>
<p>    Total income			6,476.6  vs 6,280.1</p>
<p>    - Premiums + contributions    4,838.4  vs 4,753.5</p>
<p>    - Investments		     1,568.8  vs 1,476.3</p>
<p>    - Fee income from banking	  24.8  vs    17.0</p>
<p>    - Other income			 44.6  vs    33.3</p>
<p>    Total expenses		    6,105.8  vs 5,975.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			370.8  vs   304.4</p>
<p>    Tax					51.5  vs    33.3</p>
<p>Breakdown of premium income</p>
<p>    - Life				1,229.7  vs 1,236.8</p>
<p>    - Non-life			    923.9  vs   895.1</p>
<p>    - Health (incl. constrib.)    2,684.8  vs 2,621.6</p>
<p>Note - Unlisted Achmea Holding NV, partner in the Eureko group with four other European insurance companies, said it expected to do well in the second half of 1996 and to post a higher full-year profit.</p>
<p>The Eureko venture groups Achmea, Britain's Friends Provident and Swedish Wasa and bourse-listed Portugese BCP and Danish Topdanmark.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 fax 31 20 504 5040</p>
